# Function extensionality, exercised at the surface. The dependent kernel's equality is OBSERVATIONAL: the identity type
# at a function type COMPUTES to the pointwise identity (`Id ((x:A) -> B) f g` reduces to `(x:A) -> Id B (f x) (g x)`),
# so two functions are equal exactly when they agree at every point, and funext is derivable (it is the identity), not a
# postulated axiom. This file proves two functions EQUAL AS FUNCTIONS through that mechanism: `calm` discharges the
# function equality by the kernel applying both functions to a fresh point and reducing. This is the QTT + observational
# kernel (judge.ts) showing through into form.tree, not just a value-level fact. (Pointwise equalities that are not
# definitional are proved as `mark`-quantified value laws and lifted by funext once the surface exposes a funext tactic.)

form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read prior
              read b

# add-zero-left n = 0 + n. Pointwise it equals n, definitionally (plus matches its first argument).
task add-zero-left
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  send back
    call plus
      make zero
      read n

# the identity function on the naturals.
task identity
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  send back
    read n

# FUNCTION EXTENSIONALITY: `0 + (-)` and the identity function are EQUAL AS FUNCTIONS. Not "equal at a given n" (a value
# law), but the two function values themselves identical, proved through the kernel's computing funext.
rule add-zero-left-is-identity-function
  show hold
    call is-equal
      read add-zero-left
      read identity
  calm hold

# the same point made through a second writing: `0 + (0 + n)` as a function is still the identity (funext composes).
task add-zero-twice
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  send back
    call plus
      make zero
      call plus
        make zero
        read n

rule add-zero-twice-is-identity-function
  show hold
    call is-equal
      read add-zero-twice
      read identity
  calm hold

# A NON-definitional function extensionality: `(-) + 0` and the identity function are equal as functions, even though
# `n + 0` does NOT reduce to `n` definitionally (plus recurses on its first argument). The pointwise law is proved by
# induction, then the `melt` tactic LIFTS it to the function equality through the kernel's funext. This is the funext
# tactic: a pointwise equality, however deeply proved, becomes an equality of the functions themselves.
task add-zero-right
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  send back
    call plus
      read n
      make zero

rule add-zero-right-pointwise
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call add-zero-right
        read n
      call identity
        read n
  fold n

rule add-zero-right-is-identity-function
  show hold
    call is-equal
      read add-zero-right
      read identity
  melt add-zero-right-pointwise
